1. She previously passed her theory driving test in England but failed to take the practical test within the two-year validity period due to the pandemic and lockdowns. (Verbatim: "I passed my theory, but if you pass your theory test in England, you only have two years after your theory test to then do your practical. And I didn't get to do the practical and also Covid happened and lockdown and no driving lessons... My theory test certificate has expired so I would have to redo it.")

2. She has attempted the UK driving theory test, which includes a hazard perception section involving video simulations where one must click on potential hazards without spam-clicking. (Verbatim: "The test has a question part and the other part is a simulation where you have a point of view of you driving in a car and you have to like click on the hazards... you can't spam click because it will give you like negative negative like marks for over clicking.")

